```lean
theorem linearDecay_uninhabited {X} [MeasurableSpace X] {μ : Measure X}
    (E : ℝ → EntropyData X μ) (c : LinearDecayCertificate E) : False := by
  have hb := c.cert.lower_le 0 le_rfl
  -- from time_le at t = max ((E 0).F - c.cert.lowerBound)/c.rate + 1
  set t := max (((E 0).F - c.cert.lowerBound) / c.rate) 0 + 1 with ht
  have ht0 : 0 ≤ t := by positivity  -- maybe
  have hle := c.time_le ht0
  have : ((E 0).F - c.cert.lowerBound) / c.rate < t := by simp [t]  -- linarith
  linarith
```
Careful: time_le requires t ≥ 0 and gives t ≤ C. With t = max C 0 + 1 > C. So contradiction. `linarith` should do it with le_max_left.

Also for any c, `False`, so `IsEmpty (LinearDecayCertificate E)`.

